<title>USA: American restructures Boeing order.</title>
<headline>American restructures Boeing order.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMR Corp's American Airlines said Wendesday it has restructured a $6-billion-plus order for Boeing Co planes made in November. The changes stem from the loss of certain aircraft delivery positions due to the delay in securing a new job contract with its pilots.</p>
<p>In a statement, American said it confirmed orders for 75 Boeing 737s, 12 Boeing 757s and four Boeing 767-300ERs. It said that although it remains committed to the new Boeing 777, it has not yet decided on which series to order.</p>
<p>Pilots at AMR ratified a new five-year contract Monday.</p>
